A0. COMMON PATH: every customer message goes IN and OUT this way
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[IN]
 Customer sends anything on WhatsApp
 │  WhatsApp → Meta → POST https://<domain>/webhook   (on the server, Caddy forwards it to the client's container)
 ▼
 └► app/main.py                       app                 sends /webhook to the WhatsApp router
 └► app/whatsapp/webhook.py           receive_webhook()   checks Meta's signature (WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET)
                                                          ↳ fake messages from anyone else get 401
     └► parse_webhook()                                   pulls out messages, ignores delivery/read receipts
     └► app/whatsapp/messages.py      Incoming            text / button tap / list pick → one shape
     └► queues process_incoming() as a background task, answers Meta 200 OK at once
                                                          ↳ Meta never re-sends while the AI is thinking
 └► app/services/conversation.py      process_incoming()  runs on a thread from the pool
     └► app/services/container.py     get_services()      engine, AI, CRM, translator (built at startup)
     └► _user_locks[wa_id]                                one message per customer at a time
                                                          ↳ 3 quick messages are answered in turn
     └► app/db.py                     session_scope()     one transaction: all saved or nothing
     └► app/models.py                 User, Message       finds/creates the customer, logs the message
                                                          ↳ every chat can be read later (admin API)
     └► same message again?   → A14 (stop)
     └► human has the chat?   → A9
     └► not text?             → A11
 └► app/journeys/engine.py            handle()            new customer? shortcut word? else current step
     └► app/journeys/flows/demo.yaml  (in memory)         the conversation script (client bot: main.yaml)
     └► app/i18n/translator.py + locales/<lang>.yaml      every bot sentence in the customer's language
     └► app/demo/niches.py + demo/niches.yaml             fills {business}, {book_label}, {examples}...
         ... the step-specific part: A1 to A13 ...
[OUT]
 └► app/services/conversation.py      saves each bot reply as a Message, commits
 └► app/whatsapp/client.py            mark_read()         customer sees blue ticks
                                      send()              build_payloads(): text (split at 4096 chars),
                                                          up to 3 buttons, or a list
                                                          ↳ the reply appears in the customer's chat


A1. FIRST MESSAGE FROM A NEW CUSTOMER   ("hi", or even a question)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 [A0 IN]
 └► app/models.py                     User created: no language, no step yet
 └► app/journeys/engine.py            handle(): no current step → goto("language")  (the flow's `start`)
     └► _render_languages()           one row per locales/<lang>.yaml in SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES
     └► app/i18n/translator.py        t("language.prompt")
 [A0 OUT]  "🌐 Please choose your language." + list
 ↳ every new customer picks a language first, even if their first message was a question
 (a returning customer whose step was removed from the YAML goes to the main menu instead)


A2. PICKS A LANGUAGE   (taps "हिन्दी", or types "Hindi" / "हिन्दी")
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 [A0 IN]
 └► app/journeys/engine.py            _handle_input() → language_select → _match_language()
                                      no match → the language list is sent again
 └► app/models.py                     User.language = "hi"
 └► app/i18n/translator.py            t("language.set") from locales/hi.yaml
 └► engine.goto(next)                 demo: "niche" → _render_niches() (the A3 list)
                                      client bot: "welcome" → main_menu
     └► app/demo/niches.py            Niche.text("title" / "description", "hi") via pick()
                                      (niches.yaml has only en + hi: other languages get English)
 [A0 OUT]  "language set" + the business-type list
 ↳ from now on bot sentences come from locales/hi.yaml, and the AI is told "Reply language: Hindi"
 ⚠ typing "hi" here is the shortcut word for the menu, not Hindi → menu with no business picked (A10)


A3. PICKS A BUSINESS TYPE   (demo only: taps "Clinic / Dental", types "I run a dental clinic", or "1")
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 [A0 IN]
 └► app/journeys/engine.py            _handle_input() → niche_select → _match_niche()
     └► app/demo/niches.py            Niche.matches(): id, title or an alias word
                                      first match in file order wins ("hotel restaurant" → Restaurant)
                                      no match → "Sorry, I didn't catch that" + list again
 └► app/models.py                     User.journey_data = {niche: "clinic", niche_from: <this message id>}
 └► engine.goto("niche_welcome")      message: t("demo.welcome") + Niche.params()
                                      → {business} {niche_title} {examples}
 └► engine.goto("main_menu")          menu: _render_menu() → 5 rows, row 2 title = booking.label
 [A0 OUT]  2 messages: "For this demo I'm the assistant of *SmileCare...*" + menu list
 ↳ the prospect sees the bot working for THEIR kind of business; AI memory of an earlier niche is dropped


A4. TAPS A MENU OPTION   (or types its number "1"-"5" or its exact title)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 [A0 IN]
 └► app/journeys/engine.py            _handle_input() → menu → _match_option()
                                      typed text that matches no option → the AI answers it (A5)
 └► engine.goto(option.next)          the option's next step in demo.yaml:
       Ask a question       → ai_chat_intro (t("demo.ai_intro") + examples) → ai_chat (waits)
       Book appointment     → book_name ("May I have your name, please?")   → A6
       Talk to a human      → handoff                                       → A8
       Get this bot 🚀      → pitch (signed with BUSINESS_NAME) → prospect_name → A6
       Try another business → niche list                                    → A3
     client bot (main.yaml): Ask a question · Book a demo → lead_name (A6) · My account (A13)
                             Talk to a human (A8) · Change language (A2)
 [A0 OUT]
 ↳ every option is just "go to node X" in the YAML: change the menu without touching Python


A5. TYPES A QUESTION → AI ANSWER   ("How much is a root canal?")
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 [A0 IN]
 └► app/journeys/engine.py            _handle_input(): at main_menu (no option matched → fallback ai_chat)
                                      or already in ai_chat; marks the message ai=True (it becomes memory)
 └► app/llm/assistant.py              AIAssistant.answer()
     └► _history()                    last 10 AI questions + answers from app/models.py Message
                                      (only since niche_from, so a switched niche starts fresh)
                                      ↳ follow-ups like "and for kids?" make sense
     └► build_user_turn()
         └► app/rag/retriever.py      BM25Retriever.search(question, top 4, scope="clinic")
                                      searches demo/knowledge/clinic/ + files in the top folder only
                                      (chunks were built by app/rag/ingest.py at startup)
                                      ↳ finds "Root canal treatment (RCT): ₹4,500 – ₹7,000..." in clinic.md
         └► adds "Business you represent: SmileCare..." and "Reply language: Hindi"
     └► system prompt                 demo/system_prompt.md, read once at startup
                                      (client bot: prompts/system_prompt.md)
                                      ↳ short, friendly, never invents prices, sends bookings to the menu
     └► app/llm/claude.py             ClaudeLLM.complete()   (LLM_PROVIDER=groq → app/llm/groq.py)
                                      API error → t("ai.unavailable") · refusal → t("ai.refusal")
 [A0 OUT]  reply saved with ai=True
 ↳ the customer gets the business's real price, in their own language, 24×7


A6. ANSWERS A FORM QUESTION
    demo booking: name → detail → when · Get this bot: name → business & city
    client "Book a demo": name → email → interest
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 [A0 IN]
 └► app/journeys/engine.py            _handle_input() → input
                                      empty → t("common.text_only")
                                      VALIDATORS fails (nonempty / email / phone / otp)
