A13. "MY ACCOUNT" WITH EMAIL-CODE LOGIN   (client bot only, main.yaml)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 ① taps "My account"                                           [A0 IN]
 └► app/journeys/engine.py            goto("account") → node has requires_auth: true
     └► app/auth/otp.py               AuthService.is_verified()? no → remembers auth_return = "account"
 └► engine.goto("auth_email")         input: t("auth.ask_email") "🔒 ... enter the email address registered with us"
                                                               [A0 OUT]
 ② types the email (checked by the "email" validator)          [A0 IN]
 └► engine.goto("auth_send")          action → app/journeys/actions.py send_otp()
     └► app/auth/otp.py               AuthService.start()
         └► app/crm/providers.py      find_customer_by_email()  (Customer table, or HubSpot contacts)
                                      not found → t("auth.not_found") → menu
         └► app/models.py             OtpCode: hashed 6-digit code, valid 10 min, older codes cancelled
         └► smtp_delivery()           emails the code (no SMTP_HOST → printed in the log)
     └► t("auth.otp_sent")            "We've emailed a 6-digit code to j***@example.com"
                                                               [A0 OUT]
 ③ types the code                                              [A0 IN]
 └► engine.goto("auth_verify")        action → actions.py verify_otp() → otp.py AuthService.verify()
       right  → User.customer_ref + verified_until (24 h) → "Verified ✅" → _return → "account"
                └► actions.py account_summary() → providers.py get_customer()
                   → "*Your account* Name / Email / Plan / Status" → menu
       wrong  → "That code is incorrect. Attempts left: N" (asks again)
       expired, or 5 wrong → menu
                                                               [A0 OUT]
 ④ later types "logout"
 └► engine command → actions.py logout() → otp.py AuthService.logout() → "You've been signed out." → menu
 ↳ only the real account holder sees their plan and status; no passwords are ever asked on WhatsApp


A14. META RE-SENDS A MESSAGE, OR SENDS DELIVERY / READ RECEIPTS
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 Re-sent message (same message id):
 └► app/services/conversation.py → app/models.py   Message.wa_message_id is unique → IntegrityError
     → logged "Duplicate webhook delivery ... ignored" → STOP, nothing sent
 Receipts ("delivered" / "read" for the bot's own messages):
 └► app/whatsapp/webhook.py           parse_webhook() finds no messages → nothing queued → 200 OK
 ↳ a customer never gets the same answer twice


A15. SOMETHING BREAKS WHILE ANSWERING   (database down, a bug, an action crashes)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 Inside an action:
 └► app/journeys/engine.py            _enter() catches it → t("common.error") → home menu (chat continues)
 Anywhere else in process_incoming():
 └► app/db.py                         session_scope() rolls back: nothing half-saved
 └► app/services/conversation.py      logs it, sends t("common.error") right away
                                      "Something went wrong on our side 😕 Please try again in a moment."
 ↳ the customer always gets a reply, even when something fails
 ⚠ this second case always answers in the default language (the customer's language isn't passed)


